# Meta / Instagram OAuth Checklist

Instagram OAuth integration has **six independent failure points** that each produce vague errors. Before debugging, verify ALL of these in order.

## Pre-Flight Checklist

| # | Check | Where to verify | Failure symptom |
|---|-------|----------------|-----------------|
| 1 | **App ID is correct (16 digits)** | `.env` → `INSTAGRAM_APP_ID` / `FACEBOOK_APP_ID` vs Meta Developer Dashboard | `Invalid Client ID`, `Verify failed: 400` |
| 2 | **Redirect URI matches exactly** | Backend `get_oauth_url()` output vs Meta Dashboard → Facebook Login → Settings → Valid OAuth Redirect URIs | `redirect_uri mismatch`, silent 400 |
| 3 | **App is Published** (not in Development) | Meta Dashboard → App Review → App Status toggle | OAuth dialog shows "App not set up" or blank |
| 4 | **Data Deletion URL is configured** | Meta Dashboard → App Settings → Basic → Data Deletion Callback URL | Can't publish the app without it |
| 5 | **`config_id` is included in OAuth URL** | `instagram.py` → `get_oauth_url()` params | "This content isn't available" in OAuth dialog |
| 6 | **Scopes use `instagram_business_*` naming** | `instagram.py` → scope string | Permissions silently denied |
| 7 | **API version is current** | `instagram.py` → `META_API_VERSION` | Deprecated endpoint errors |

